  "title": "CANDOR: Chance-Calibrated Discordance in Frozen Foundation Encoders",
  "summary": "CANDOR introduces a discordance measure that fixes the chance level at exactly half, correcting previous conclusions about frozen encoders. The method reverses the idea that a frozen encoder is blind, while showing that it is still weak and performs well in certain tasks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "CANDOR fixes the chance level at exactly half, which corrects previous conclusions about frozen encoders.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Across 22 encoders and 605,443 images, the method reverses the idea that a frozen encoder is blind.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The best chest model reads pneumothorax at 84.5 AUROC and still places 18.4% of positives nearer an opposite-label film than its own kind in the same hospital.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
